WEBVTT

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:05.337
This section is a brief overview
about tinnitus, what it is,

00:00:05.377 --> 00:00:09.380
possible causes of tinnitus,
and how common it is.

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:13.640
This section will also cover what
can and cannot be done for tinnitus.

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.253
The most important
audiological tip related

00:00:16.293 --> 00:00:20.340
to tinnitus will also be
covered in this section.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:23.720
So what is tinnitus?

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:28.266
Typically, sound is produced
by vibrations in the air

00:00:28.306 --> 00:00:32.440
being coded and interpreted
by our brains as sound.

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:35.363
But the sound of tinnitus
that you may be experiencing

00:00:35.403 --> 00:00:38.420
is not caused by external
sound vibrations.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:45.020
Instead, the noise of most forms of tinnitus
is an internally experienced sound.

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:49.272
That internal tinnitus noise
is created by some of your nerve

00:00:49.312 --> 00:00:54.760
fibers firing and the brain
interpreting those signals as sound.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:59.083
Tinnitus can be experienced
as different kinds of sounds,

00:00:59.123 --> 00:01:02.825
ranging from a ringing,
a high pitched tone, hissing,

00:01:02.865 --> 00:01:07.720
a noise like a high tension wire,
a buzzing or a sizzling.

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:13.460
One individual can experience multiple
kinds of tinnitus related sounds.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:17.594
Most kinds of tinnitus
are symptoms of neural

00:01:17.634 --> 00:01:21.600
damage and not the actual
disease by itself.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:26.120
Some use the term sensorineural reaction.

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:29.498
See the website listed
on the PowerPoint slide

00:01:29.538 --> 00:01:33.160
if you want more
information about that term.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:37.907
Subjective tinnitus reflects
that neurological damage was

00:01:37.947 --> 00:01:42.000
done most likely along
the auditory nerve in the brain.

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:46.960
That is why surgery or other
kinds of cures may not work.

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:52.580
That is, subjective tinnitus is a symptom
and not the primary condition causing

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:58.540
you to experience ringing or hissing
or other sounds that you may experience.

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:04.210
This is a brief note
on the structure of the ear.

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:11.510
The ear consists of three major parts,
the outer ear, middle ear, and inner ear.

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:14.512
In the inner ear,
there is a fluid filled structure

00:02:14.552 --> 00:02:18.430
that is shaped like a snail
shell called the cochlea.

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:23.530
Its function is to convert sound wave
vibrations into electrical signals.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:26.876
These electrical signals then
travel along the auditory

00:02:26.916 --> 00:02:30.970
or hearing nerve into the brain
to be interpreted as sound.

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:33.901
The auditory nerve,
like other nerves in our bodies,

00:02:33.941 --> 00:02:36.650
can be damaged by a variety of things.

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:39.062
Because of the complexity
of neural networking,

00:02:39.102 --> 00:02:42.210
it is difficult to pinpoint
the place of damage.

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:45.222
This is why you should always
be checked by a medical doctor

00:02:45.262 --> 00:02:48.470
with the onset of tinnitus in order
to rule out the possibility

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:51.750
of underlying medical
conditions causing tinnitus.

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:56.729
For most but not all people, tinnitus
is a reflection of damage to auditory

00:02:56.769 --> 00:03:01.330
nerves or elsewhere within the hearing
nervous system of the brain.

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:05.410
The nerves in our brains are networked.

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:07.590
This is called neural networking.

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:11.930
The nerve fibers branch out as they
travel from the auditory nerve

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:16.530
toward the cerebral cortex,
which is the outer layer of the brain.

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:19.201
Because the brain contains
neural networking,

00:03:19.241 --> 00:03:24.210
it is difficult to know exactly
where that neural damage occurred.

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:27.495
If the location of the nerve
damage could be pinpointed,

00:03:27.535 --> 00:03:32.850
finding a treatment or even a cure
for tinnitus symptoms might be easier.

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:38.910
Scientific research and clinical
practice have not reached this point yet.

00:03:40.710 --> 00:03:43.570
So, what can cause tinnitus?

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:48.430
Things that may cause hearing
loss may also cause tinnitus.

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:51.659
The most common cause
of tinnitus is loud noise,

00:03:51.699 --> 00:03:56.270
such as gunshots, explosions,
or even very loud rock music.

00:03:56.570 --> 00:03:59.352
Some researchers noted
that the length of exposure time

00:03:59.392 --> 00:04:03.870
to occupational and leisure noise
was related to rates of tinnitus.

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:04.959
See Bott, Harrison,

00:04:04.999 --> 00:04:08.910
and Lynn article and reference
file if you want more information.

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:12.349
Because tinnitus is related
to exposure to loud noise,

00:04:12.389 --> 00:04:17.310
it is important to protect your ears
and hearing from further damage.

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:22.086
And this is an important message to explain
to others, especially those who like

00:04:22.126 --> 00:04:27.210
to crank up the volume of their favorite
music and listen to it using earphones.

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:32.341
Other tinnitus causes can
include head or neck injury,

00:04:32.381 --> 00:04:35.250
earwax, some prescription drugs.

00:04:35.570 --> 00:04:40.651
A professional tinnitus association,
namely the American Tinnitus Association,

00:04:40.691 --> 00:04:44.850
indicated that there may be
around 200 causes of tinnitus.

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:49.814
See the website link listed on this
PowerPoint slide if you need more information.

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:55.090
You should always be checked by a medical
doctor with the onset of tinnitus.

00:04:55.220 --> 00:04:57.169
A doctor should rule out the possibility

00:04:57.209 --> 00:05:00.630
of underlying medical
conditions causing tinnitus.

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:04.939
For most, but not all, people,
tinnitus is a reflection of damage

00:05:04.979 --> 00:05:09.770
to auditory nerves or elsewhere within
the nervous system of the brain.

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:14.796
Please see the course disclaimer in section
one slides four and five for information

00:05:14.836 --> 00:05:19.790
about when you should seek immediate
medical care for the onset of tinnitus.

00:05:20.010 --> 00:05:22.823
Sometimes tinnitus may
be connected with medical

00:05:22.863 --> 00:05:25.690
issues that need immediate treatment.

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:29.610
How common is tinnitus?

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:34.915
Representative studies show that worldwide,
tinnitus occurs in about

00:05:34.955 --> 00:05:39.890
3 to 36 percent of the population,
depending on the type of study.

00:05:40.010 --> 00:05:43.190
This is from a study
published by Deshaies et al.

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:45.930
2005, See Course Reference List.

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:50.929
A 2016 study by Bhatt,
Lin and Bhattacharyya, 2016,

00:05:50.969 --> 00:05:54.790
indicates that approximately
10 percent of the U.S.

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:58.420
population experiences
tinnitus and that of that 36

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:02.290
percent experience constant
symptoms of tinnitus.

00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:05.563
The other people reporting
tinnitus in that study experienced

00:06:05.603 --> 00:06:09.390
symptoms that were intermittent
or that stopped for a while.

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:13.850
Thus, tinnitus is quite common
among the general population.

00:06:14.050 --> 00:06:17.590
It is the number one service-connected
disability among U.S.

00:06:17.630 --> 00:06:21.250
veterans and has been
for more than a decade.
